====Usage notes====
* The term "First Lady" was not used until the funeral of {{w|Dolley Madison}} in 1849, the wife of President {{w|James Madison}} (whose term was 1809-1817), by then-President {{w|Zachary Taylor}}, for the wife of a president of the United States.<ref> History Channel; [https://www.history.com/topics/first-ladies/dolley-madison "Dolley Madison"]; eds. History.com; 9 November 2009 </ref><ref name=SScom> SoftSchools.com; [https://www.softschools.com/language_arts/reading_comprehension/social_studies/373/first_ladies_of_the_white_house/ "First Ladies of the White House"]  </ref><ref name=ISBN-9781929175093>{{cite-book|first=Richard N. |last=Côté |title=Strength and Honor: The Life of Dolley Madison |publisher=Corinthian Books |year=2005 |isbn=9781929175093 |page=261}}</ref>

